  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_f8193cafdf8e48b29ffd077bc8c105d2",
      "statement": "The merge endpoint (POST /api/tasks/:taskId/merge-pr) is the only endpoint that combines a sandbox teardown (Sandbox.get + sandbox.stop + unregisterSandbox) with writing completedAt on the tasks row, and it does so even when the task's keepAlive flag is true. A single UPDATE writes prStatus='merged', prMergeCommitSha, sandboxId=NULL, sandboxUrl=NULL, completedAt=now, updatedAt. The route catches and logs (but does not surface) errors from the sandbox teardown so a transient stop failure does not roll back the merge that GitHub has already accepted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/%5BtaskId%5D/merge-pr/route.ts#L57-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b65787f130730962df3273dfe7ccc43a720458b3a8c05dbff2abd9b64b3d397a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/%5BtaskId%5D/merge-pr/route.ts#L66-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a7fd4f51d2bf5943d64be89f0fa8c5dce6dc25aff6a4b0229d3c93581b516da4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_21843d42887243cca13f9d8eafee050a",
      "statement": "POST /api/tasks/:taskId/pr is idempotent: if task.prUrl is already set, the handler returns 200 with data.alreadyExists=true without contacting the GitHub API. This means re-clicking the Open PR button on an existing task safely surfaces the existing PR (the client routes to the merge dialog) and recovering from a transient network failure between GitHub's 201 Created and the local UPDATE never creates a second PR.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/%5BtaskId%5D/pr/route.ts#L46-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3937bbaaee9d29cb90febe11fa5a837863fb405ab1a3842f50e3166173407945:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bef5e8cf5e7f467c9c3cece55dd8123d",
      "statement": "POST /api/tasks/:taskId/sync-pr is the second of the three places completedAt is written: when getPullRequestStatus returns status='merged', the route's UPDATE sets prStatus, prMergeCommitSha, and completedAt=now in a single statement. The first writer is the merge endpoint itself; the third is PATCH /api/tasks/:taskId with action='stop'. The worker's success path (logger.updateStatus('completed')) deliberately does not set completedAt.",
