    {
      "id": "claim_96d0aac648ed40de839ea28b3c35e570",
      "statement": "The close-pr and reopen-pr routes are thin wrappers over octokit.rest.pulls.update with state='closed' or state='open'. Neither route writes completedAt: closing is treated as a reversible state change rather than a terminal status, and reopening restores prStatus='open' without disturbing the row's prior completedAt. They share the same 401/403/404/500 status-code translations and both return 400 'Task does not have a pull request' when repoUrl or prNumber is missing.",
      "evidence": [
